      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both approaches lead to the same (optimal) codegen. Below `%ymm4` maps to `dr`, `(%rax)` is `stack[0]`, `32(%rax)` is `stack[1]`. I actually wrote it your way at first and then decided `stack[0] \u0026 stack[1]` was easier to read, but I can change it if you want to be explicit about using the register.\n\n```\n    d760: 48 8b 46 08                  \tmovq\t8(%rsi), %rax\n    d764: c5 fc 11 60 20               \tvmovups\t%ymm4, 32(%rax)\n    d769: c5 dc 54 20                  \tvandps\t(%rax), %ymm4, %ymm4\n    d76d: 48 8b 46 10                  \tmovq\t16(%rsi), %rax\n    d771: 48 83 c6 10                  \taddq\t$16, %rsi\n    d775: ff e0                        \tjmpq\t*%rax\n```",
